From: cormierjohn <49281283+cormierjohn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:20:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] perf(compensation): flat span rows, reused buffers, skip
 depths for equal values

Rows of runs and spans now live in flat arrays indexed by row instead of one
vector per row, and each worker reuses its dilation buffers across rows. When
the outline and hole distances are equal, every edge moves the same way, so
the nesting depths are skipped: removal is the solid within the distance of
any background, addition the background within it of any solid.

On a full-plate Saturn 4 Ultra 16K layer (M5 Max), compensation now takes
about 2 ms with different distances and 1 ms with equal ones, down from 4 to
4.6 ms; with the raster included the layer goes from 3.1-3.8 ms to 1.2-1.6 ms
(raster alone 0.27 ms). Output is identical to the previous version on that
layer for six settings, and the pixel-reference test now covers equal values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
